==Solution 5==

We will do this by area subtraction. Drawing in the required lines, we drop an altitude from A to WZ and an altitude from E to XY. You get 2 30-60-90 triangles, and given that the side length is <imath>x</imath>, AZ is <imath>2x/3</imath>, which means that WZ is <imath>5x/3</imath>, adding in AB. Using the 30-60-90 triangle again, you get that the area of trapezoid <imath>ABWZ</imath> is <imath>\frac{4x}{3} \cdot</imath> <imath>\frac{x\sqrt3}{3}</imath>. Repeat on the other side to get that the area of both of these trapezoids combined are <imath>\frac{8x^2\sqrt3}{9}</imath>. Finding the area of the hexagon, dividing, and subtracting, gets you C.

